DAVE, Discord's end-to-end encryption of calls (MLS through libdave), compiled by the plugin build (plugin.json lists the sources) from plain
source lists, no CMake and no vcpkg. Only the sources below and the headers beside them are kept, unmodified; tests, tools, assembly and the
parts not listed are not vendored. The crypto backend is BoringSSL built with OPENSSL_NO_ASM (the same C everywhere); see the decision in
the notes of ZN-872 (BoringSSL scored above OpenSSL 3 and above a port of mlspp's hpke to mbedTLS). Its OpenSSL-named symbols (EVP_*, ...)
cannot meet the engine's mbedTLS (mbedtls_*, psa_*), and live only in this plugin's library.

